course: dictionary
lesson: 9639
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around the word, which are its context. «Stunt performers do the dangerous parts so actors stay safe.» Here the clue is dangerous parts in a film, so a stunt is a daring or dangerous action.
explain: Clues can also warn you. «Do not try this at home» tells you that stunts are planned by experts and must not be copied. Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does it still make sense?
explain: Stunt has other meanings too. «A publicity stunt» is a trick done to get attention. «The plant was stunted because it had no light» shows that to stunt something means to stop it growing properly. The clue here is the plant without light.
fact: A stunt is a daring or dangerous action, often done in a film or show.
fact: A stunt double is a trained performer who stands in for an actor in the dangerous moments.
fact: «Publicity stunt» means a trick done to get attention.
fact: «Stunted» means stopped from growing properly, as when a plant lacks light or food.
fact: Stunts are planned for weeks by experts with padding, airbags and harnesses, and even they sometimes get hurt, so stunts are never for copying at home.
exercise: «Stunt performers do the dangerous parts so actors stay safe.» What is a stunt here? | *A daring or dangerous action in a film or show | A letter sent by post | A quiet rest after lunch | A kind of cake
exercise: «The plant was stunted because it had no light.» What does stunted mean here? | Watered every day | Painted bright green | *Stopped from growing properly | Very tall and strong
exercise: What is the main purpose of a «publicity stunt»? | To keep warm | To hide from others | *To get people's attention | To pass a test
test: Why should children never copy a film stunt at home? | It is too easy to do | *Trained experts plan them with safety gear, and even they can get hurt | Films are always fake, so it is safe | Stunts only happen in the daytime
test: What is a stunt double? | A film director | A safety harness | *A trained performer who stands in for an actor in dangerous moments | An actor who never does any dangerous moments
exam: Which sentence uses stunt to mean a trick done to get attention? | The school bell rang at nine | *The shop gave away free cakes as a publicity stunt | The stunt performer jumped from the roof | The lack of light stunted the plant
